 squads takes the rating of the highest squad value in his group not above his. Then every club is moved toward its real results: S is the Simple Rating System of its 1269 games' scores from MoneyPuck.com's game files (margins by least squares with a home edge of 0.29, a shoot-out's goal left out), reliability r 0.672; m, the match model's margin a game per point of a lineup's played strength (the mean of its attack and defence) under the season's rules, is 0.3081 goals (at scoring 0.977); each club's target is the clubs' mean before the move + √r × S ÷ m, and every player of the club moves by one whole number, its best few one point more, whichever brings its lineup nearest the target (no player passes one rated above him in his club). Every player's lines and the season's results are in scripts/data/nhl-seasons/nhl-2018.json.","licence":"free to use for non-commercial purposes, crediting MoneyPuck.com (moneypuck.com/data.htm)","attribution":"Statistics from MoneyPuck.com. Where its player lookup gives no nationality, the birth country is the Hockey Databank's: \"The information used herein was obtained free of charge from and is copyrighted by the Hockey Databank project.  For more information about the Hockey Databank project please visit http://sports.groups.yahoo.com/group/hockey-databank\"","nation":"the nationality MoneyPuck.com's player lookup gives (the NHL's); where it gives none, the Hockey Databank's birth country of the one player of 2008/09 to 2017/18 with that name"},"map":"nhl2018","nations":{"124":[93,23,[["Connor McDavid","C",98],["Claude Giroux","C",97],["Nathan MacKinnon","C",96],["Sidney Crosby","C",96],["Steven Stamkos","C",94],["Mark Scheifele","C",93],["Tyler Seguin","C",93],["John Tavares","C",92],["Ryan Getzlaf","C",91],["Brayden Schenn","C",90],["Brad Marchand","LW",96],["Jamie Benn","LW",95],["Taylor Hall","LW",95],["Jaden Schwartz","LW",90],["Mark Stone","RW",89],["Brent Burns","D",96],["Drew Doughty","D",94],["Alex Pietrangelo","D",91],